WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.301
-Guys, earlier today is usually

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:03.636
when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:05.504
You know, I check my inbox,
return some e-mails,

00:00:05.504 --> 00:00:07.240
and of course, I send out
thank-you notes.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.109
And I was --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.376
I was running a bit behind,

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:11.610
so I thought if you guys
wouldn't mind,

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:12.645
I'd just like to write out

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.013
my weekly thank-you notes
right now.

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:15.081
Is that cool with you?

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.449
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.850
Thank you very much.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.087
James, can I get some thank-you-
note-writing music, please?

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.622
[ Somber piano music playing ]

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:24.890
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:27.327
Always in a good mood.

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.495
-Jimmy Baseball.
-Always in a good mood. Okay.

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:31.497
[ Piano music stops ]

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:32.865
[ Piano music restarts ]

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:34.734
Thank you, Father's Day,

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.670
for basically being Mother's Day
without the eye contact.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.240
[ Piano music stops,
laughter and applause ]

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:45.144
[ Piano music restarts ]

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:48.481
Thank you, group photo
of world leaders at NATO,

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.915
for looking like
an a cappella group

00:00:49.915 --> 00:00:52.551
that lasts just eight seconds
on "America's Got Talent."

00:00:52.551 --> 00:00:54.120
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.855
-[ Imitates buzzer ]

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:01.026
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:01.026 --> 00:01:04.130
-[ Vocalizing ]

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.266
-[ Imitates buzzer ]
[ The Roots vocalizing ]

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.837
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:12.205
♪♪

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.073
-Thank you...
-What -- What was that?

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.042
-...Novavax -- What's that?

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.477
-What was that?
-Dude, it's like out of nowhere,

00:01:18.477 --> 00:01:19.745
you can just make
an a cappella group.

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:21.114
-Really?

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:24.850
-♪ The very first time ♪

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:27.420
[ The Roots vocalizing ]

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.422
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.422 --> 00:01:31.624
-Well, not every time.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.192
-Not every time.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:34.427
-Most times.
-Most times.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.796
-Yeah, yeah. Sure.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.331
-♪ Your lips said hello ♪

00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:40.999
♪ And I said hi ♪

00:01:40.999 --> 00:01:43.069
-[ Vocalizes off-key ]

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.504
-I guess just one time.

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.305
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.305 --> 00:01:47.806
[ Piano music restarts ]

00:01:47.806 --> 00:01:51.878
-Thank you, Novavax releasing
an effective vaccine this week,

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:53.212
for basically being that guy

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:55.748
who shows up to a party
with a six-pack at 4:00 a.m.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.850
It's like, "Novavax!

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.252
You rock!"

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.588
[ Applause ]

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:06.225
♪ But I was caught up ♪

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:08.995
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:10.329
1, 2 --

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:11.897
♪ But I was caught up ♪
-♪ Caught up ♪

00:02:11.897 --> 00:02:14.634
-There you go.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.002
♪♪

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:18.304
-Thank you,
Biden and Putin summit,

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.039
for looking like
all of us with our dads

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.674
10 minutes into Father's Day.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:22.709
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:24.510
So, uh --

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:25.745
Family good?

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:26.846
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:28.080
Yeah.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.850
They're great.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.085
♪♪

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.153
Thank you, spray sunscreen,

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:37.390
for being the closest I'll ever
get to graffiti-ing my family.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.826
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:42.728
-[ Imitating spraying ]

00:02:42.728 --> 00:02:45.130
[ Imitating spray can shaking ]

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:47.467
[ Imitating spraying ]

00:02:49.535 --> 00:02:50.637
"Biscuit"?

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.805
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.674
-Yeah, that's my
graffiti name, Biscuit.

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.909
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:58.077
♪♪

00:02:58.077 --> 00:02:59.679
-Thank you, Brooklyn Nets,

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:03.382
for being the most exciting team
with the least exciting name.

00:03:03.382 --> 00:03:05.318
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:07.754
That's right. We're the Nets!

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:11.324
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.324 --> 00:03:12.991
♪♪

00:03:12.991 --> 00:03:14.961
Thank you, seashells,

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.929
for showing up
in one of two places --

00:03:16.929 --> 00:03:19.932
a beautiful shoreline
or a bowl on your aunt's toilet.

00:03:19.932 --> 00:03:21.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.002
Classic.
-Classic.

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:25.505
-Classic.
-It's if you run out of paper.

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.040
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.041
-That's not why it's there.

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:30.843
-That's not why?
-If you run out of paper?

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.411
No. That's not why it's there.

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:34.680
-You have a shell, you know?
-No, no, no.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.449
-Are you sure?

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:37.683
♪♪

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:39.485
-Thank you, hang gliding,

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.620
for being my favorite way
to see stunning views

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:44.089
while dangling from
an oversized Dorito.

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:46.492
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:51.697
This is a good one.

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:53.399
-[ Inhales sharply ]
[ Piano music restarts ]

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:56.235
-Thank you, ice cream trucks,
for being the only time

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:58.470
where I'm like, "Kids, hurry!
Run into the street

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:01.674
and buy sweets
from a stranger in a van."

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.209
There you have it.
Those are my thank-you notes.

